-- title:
--   Sections of n base-point-free bundles avoiding a small closed set
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an infinite field and let $V$ be a scheme with a morphism $\pi \colon V \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, whose underlying topological space is Noetherian. Let $n$ be a natural number and let $N_0,\dots,N_{n-1}$ be $\mathcal{O}_V$-modules, each invertible in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible`: for every point $x \in V$ there is an open $U \ni x$ such that the pullback of $N_i$ along the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow V$ is isomorphic to the unit module of $U$. Assume each $N_i$ is base-point free in the following sense: for every $i$ and every $x \in V$ there is a global section $s \colon \mathcal{O}_V \to N_i$ with $x$ outside the support of `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s`, the smallest ideal sheaf datum $J$ on $V$ with $J.\mathrm{ideal}(U)$ containing, for every affine open $U$, the ideal generated by all coefficients of $s$ over $U$. Let $B \subseteq V$ be closed, with $\mathrm{topologicalKrullDim}\, B < n$, the supremum of lengths of chains of irreducible closed subsets of $B$ being less than $n$. Then there is a family of global sections $s_i \colon \mathcal{O}_V \to N_i$, $0 \le i < n$, such that $B$ meets the intersection of the supports of the ideal sheaves $\mathrm{zeroSchemeIdeal}(s_i)$ in the empty set.
--
--   This is an avoidance lemma of Kleiman's type: over an infinite field, base-point-free invertible sheaves have global sections whose common zero locus misses a prescribed closed subset of dimension less than the number of sheaves. It is used in the study of the relative group law on Jacobians, in the argument `coeff_eq_zero_of_not_isFinite_endKerStr_of_forall_eulerChar_tensorPow_eq` on Euler characteristics of tensor powers.
